# Neo Drive parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoDrive
namespace NeoBuzz.Drive
class NeoDriveMachine
summary Saturator: tape, tube, transistor, diode and wavefolder models with bias, tone filters, auto gain and oversampling. Use it for warmth and grit on tracks, glue on buses, or as a distortion effect.

group Drive
Mode       "Mode"       0 4    0    enum Tape Tube Transistor Diode Fold | Saturation model
    how Chooses the saturation model: Tape, Tube, Transistor, Diode or Fold.
    sound Tape is soft and warm, Tube is rich and full, Transistor is firmer, Diode is edgy and Fold is bright and metallic.
Drive      "Drive"      0 1000 250  lin 0 36 dB 1          | Gain into the saturation
    how Raises the level going into the saturation by 0 to 36 dB.
    sound More drive adds harmonics, going from a subtle warmth to heavy distortion.
Bias       "Bias"       0 1000 500  bip                    | Shifts the curve off centre: even harmonics
    how Shifts the signal off centre before the saturation.
    sound Pushing it away from the middle adds even harmonics, which sound fuller and more asymmetric.
Character  "Character"  0 1000 500  pct                    | Tape: emphasis. Tube: sag. Transistor: hardness. Diode: asymmetry. Fold: folds
    how Sets the model's special trait: tape emphasis, tube sag, transistor hardness, diode asymmetry or fold amount.
    sound Higher values make each model more pronounced and more obviously coloured.
group Tone
LowCut     "Low cut"    0 1000 0    freq 10 1000           | High-pass before the saturation
    how Filters the low frequencies, from 10 Hz to 1 kHz, out of the signal before it is saturated.
    sound Bass stops overloading the saturation, so the result is tighter and less muddy.
Tone       "Tone"       0 1000 500  bip                    | Tilt after the saturation: darker or brighter
    how Tilts the tone after the saturation, darker towards the left and brighter towards the right.
    sound Turn it down to soften harsh distortion; turn it up for more sparkle.
HighCut    "High cut"   0 1000 1000 freq 1000 22000        | Low-pass after the saturation
    how Removes frequencies above 1 to 22 kHz after the saturation.
    sound Lower values tame fizz and harshness, making the drive darker and smoother.
group Output
Output     "Output"     0 1000 500  db -24 24              | Output level
    how Sets the final level in dB, from -24 to +24.
    sound It makes the sound louder or quieter without changing the amount of distortion.
AutoGain   "Auto gain"  0 1    1    switch                 | Holds the level steady as the drive changes
    how Keeps the output level steady as Drive changes.
    sound You hear the character change rather than a simple volume increase.
Mix        "Mix"        0 1000 1000 pct                    | Dry/wet (the dry signal is delayed to match)
    how Blends the saturated signal with the dry signal, delayed to match.
    sound Lower values keep the original punch and add the saturation as a subtle layer.
Quality    "Quality"    0 2    1    enum 2× 4× 8×          | Oversampling
    how Chooses the oversampling: 2x, 4x or 8x.
    sound Higher settings keep high-frequency distortion clean and free of aliasing, but use more processing power.
